      impressum_body: "Information according to § 5 DDG (Germany)<br><br><strong>Tetyana Bastron</strong><br>Podiatric practice approved for all statutory and private health insurances<br>Lerchenstr. 28<br>49088 Osnabrück<br><br>Phone: 0541 40722215<br>Email: podologiebastron@outlook.de<br><br>VAT identification number pursuant to § 27a of the German VAT Act: DE401739270<br><br>Professional title: State-certified podologist, conferred in Germany.<br>Approval under § 124(1) SGB V (statutory health insurance) granted by ARGE Heilmittelzulassung Niedersachsen, c/o Verband der Ersatzkassen e. V. (vdek), Schillerstraße 32, 30159 Hannover, www.zulassung-heilmittel.de<br>Member of the German Association of Podology (ZFD) e.V.<br><br>Responsible for content per § 18 Abs. 2 MStV: Tetyana Bastron (address as above).",
      datenschutz_title: "Privacy Policy",
      datenschutz_body: "<p><em>The German version is the legally binding one; this translation is for information only.</em></p>\n<h4>1. Controller</h4><p>Tetyana Bastron, Podologie Bastron<br>Lerchenstr. 28, 49088 Osnabrück, Germany<br>Phone: 0541 40722215 · Email: podologiebastron@outlook.de</p>\n<h4>2. Our website</h4>\n<p><strong>Server log files.</strong> When you visit the website, technically necessary data (IP address, date and time, page requested, browser type) is processed. The website is hosted by Netlify, Inc. (USA). Purpose: providing and securing the website; legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. For any transfer to the USA the provider relies on the applicable safeguards (e.g. standard contractual clauses).</p>\n<p><strong>No cookies, no tracking.</strong> We use no cookies, analytics or advertising services. Fonts are loaded from our own server, not from Google.</p>\n<p><strong>Language setting.</strong> Your chosen language is stored only locally in your browser. No personal data is transmitted to us.</p>\n<p><strong>Google Maps.</strong> The map is only loaded after you click \"Load map\". This transfers data (including your IP address) to Google Ireland Limited, Gordon House, Barrow Street, Dublin 4, Ireland, and possibly to Google servers in the USA. Legal basis: your consent, Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR. Without a click, nothing is transferred.</p>\n<p><strong>Contacting us.</strong> When you call or write to us, we process your details to handle your request (Art. 6(1)(b) or (f) GDPR). We book appointments by phone only. Please do not send health data by email, as emails can be read by third parties.</p>\n<p><strong>External links.</strong> The operators of linked sites (e.g. recommendations, NutriAtlas AI) are responsible for their content and privacy practices.</p>\n<h4>3. Patient data at the practice</h4>\n<p><strong>Data processed:</strong> contact details (name, address, phone, email), health data (history, findings, treatments), insurance and billing data, and where necessary data from other practitioners needed for treatment. We receive the data from you and from the doctor's prescription.</p>\n<p><strong>Legal bases:</strong> treatment contract (Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR), provision of health care (Art. 9(2)(h) GDPR in conjunction with § 22 BDSG) and legal obligations (e.g. documentation). Consent is only needed if data is used for non-medical purposes (e.g. photos for advertising).</p>\n<p><strong>Retention:</strong> patient records are kept for at least 10 years after treatment ends (§ 630f BGB) and then deleted.</p>\n<p><strong>Recipients:</strong> data is only disclosed where required by law, necessary for treatment or billing, or with your consent (e.g. doctors involved in your care, health insurers). To bill prescriptions to the health insurers, the practice works with the billing centre opta data; the practice software is provided by thevea GmbH (Essen). According to these providers, processing takes place on servers in Germany.</p>\n<p><strong>Confidentiality:</strong> I am bound by statutory professional secrecy (§ 203 StGB).</p>\n<h4>4. Your rights</h4>\n<p>You have the right to access, rectification, erasure, restriction of processing, data portability and objection. You may withdraw consent at any time with effect for the future. You may also complain to the supervisory authority: Die Landesbeauftragte für den Datenschutz Niedersachsen, Prinzenstraße 5, 30159 Hannover, Germany.</p>\n<p><em>Last updated: October 2026</em></p>"
